{
  "slug": "artist:dougal",
  "name": "Dougal",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Northampton on 14 April 1975, Paul Arnold Clarke began his career in the UK happy hardcore scene by setting up sound systems for early acid house parties at age 15. Clarke eventually became a resident DJ at major rave institutions including Dreamscape, Helter Skelter, and Equinox Milwaukees. His production work is characterized by a mix of euphoric hardcore and uplifting vocals, frequently collaborating with artists like Hixxy and Gammer. Together with Hixxy, he established the Essential Platinum label. Clarke played a significant role in the commercial success of the Bonkers compilation series, which achieved gold certification in the UK. Five of these compilations featuring his mixes reached the top 20 of the UK albums chart. He continues to perform, including appearances at the Bang Face Weekender alongside Hixxy.",
